      "transliteration": "yaccakṣuṣā na paśyati yena cakṣūm̐ṣi paśyati\ntadeva brahma tvaṁ viddhi nedaṁ yadidamupāsate",
      "translation": "What the eye cannot see — but by which the eyes see — know that alone to be Brahman, not this that people worship here.",
